From: genspark_dev <genspark_dev@genspark.ai>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 02:10:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the verification script against what the site actually
 reported
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Running it on a real bench exposed four defects, three of them in the script itself.

Report names were guessed with a like filter, so '%queue%' matched Work Queue and
Follow Up Queue and the same report was reported three times while another was never
checked. Resolve each name from its own definition on disk instead.

The hook entries carry 'name' and 'method'; the script read 'workflow_action', so
every lifecycle-hook line printed '?'.

Arabic was reported as missing because the check demanded Translation rows. App
translations load from the app's own CSV; a site with a full Arabic file and no
Translation rows is correctly translated. Check the catalogue and the ar language.

And the role script saved the Report document, which wrote the definitions back into
the app tree — configuring a site edited tracked source. Write the Has Role rows
directly, and commit explicitly, because bench execute does not.

Add the transition-task setup: a workflow_methods hook only fires through a task
attached to a transition, and plan/apply make that mapping explicit.
